{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/290566-adapting-a-creepypasta-for-wod-use","id":290566,"title":"Adapting a Creepypasta for WOD use?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-23T09:31:54-07:00","id":290566,"title":"Adapting a Creepypasta for WOD use?","content":"So, someone pointed me towards this creepypasta,<br /> <a href=\"http://creepypasta.wikia.com/wiki/1999\" target=\"_blank\">http://creepypasta.wikia.com/wiki/1999</a><br /> <br /> And it occurred to me that this might make for a good Hunter:The Reckoning story. BUT, I'm kind of lost on ideas to adapt it. i.e. getting the characters involved, what exactly Mr. Bear is, what the nature of the channel is etc. So, I'm gonna throw it out to you folks for suggestions. And has anyone adapted Creepypastas for WOD use before? How'd it go?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/nbylxup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n77xu8p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1667-novagain","name":"Novagain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T10:46:18-07:00","id":290659,"title":"","content":"Can it be done with WoD? Yes.<br /> <br /> Is it relatively easy? Also yes.<br /> <br /> Leaving the exact nature of the thing's origin up to speculation is usually best when using a non-stop creature. This doesn't go for just homemade NPC's. Some antagonist and ST characters presented in books are best left to the winds of change, when it comes to story. The classic splat books, especially the 20th Anniversary editions, Freak Legion: A Guide to Fomori, the Bygone Bestiary, the list goes on.<br /> <br /> So long as you keep true to what you like about the creature/character, you can usually mimic most powers and abilities by cherry-picking through merits and powers from your favorite splat books.<br /> Really, what matters is fitting said creepy-thingy into your story, and making it functional while still keeping the spirit of the thing alive and intact. This involves some psychology. Take the original post and expand on it. Prepare some 'prop' text documents to be sent out later as emails or messages. Have a &quot;prop bag&quot; of material you can help players get immersed in the idea that this is 'real' in your WoD.<br /> <br /> If you don't mind switching systems a bitsy, or translating mechanics, there's tons of nWoD stuff to mine for gold. Snagging a few Arcana powers, a Discipline dot here and there, rename an Uratha Gift. A few good toolboxes for nWoD besides that are Second Sight*, Antagonists and Mirrors. ...Maybe Slasher**, too.<br /> <br /> Have I ever ported a creepypasta into my WoD? Many times.<br /> <br /> I started off with things from SomethingAwful, like Slenderman and the like. It had fun moments.<br /> <br /> I haven't done much gaming lately, but I homebrew when I'm bored, so I've recently been cobbling together a few versions of this little fella:<br /> <br /> Mr. Ickbarr Bigelsteine<br /> <img src=\"http://fc09.deviantart.net/fs70/f/2013/180/2/d/ickbarr_bigelsteine_by_ebbud-d6b9rb1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> He's a Sock-Monster. You should read his story. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *Much of the Numina in Second Sight is presented in a revised form in the God-Machine Chronicle<br /> <br /> **(I have decided to include Slasher in every list of good nWoD things from now on. Favorite Hunter book? Slasher. Favorite Mage book? Slasher?Favorite Promethean book? SLASHER.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 10-23-2014, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}